# What NOT to serve, when the deployed asset directory is the repo root.
#
# The site deploys as a Cloudflare *Pages* project, which does not read this
# file — with an empty build command nothing installs, so there is no
# node_modules to leak. It is kept because a Workers deploy DOES read it, and
# that path failed exactly once already: wrangler installed itself into the
# directory being uploaded, and the 144 MiB `workerd` binary blew past
# Cloudflare's 25 MiB per-asset limit. Everything else here is simply not web
# content: it lives on GitHub, it doesn't belong on the site.

node_modules
.git
.claude

test
scripts
docs

CLAUDE.md
README.md
package.json
package-lock.json
bun.lockb
wrangler.jsonc
.assetsignore
.gitignore
preview.png
